   "id": "ketubot.47a.10",
   "daf": "47a",
   "sentenceId": 9,
   "he": "נִיסֵּת, יָתֵר עָלָיו הַבַּעַל שֶׁהוּא אוֹכֵל כּוּ׳. תָּנוּ רַבָּנַן: כָּתַב לָהּ פֵּירוֹת, כְּסוּת וְכֵלִים שֶׁיָּבוֹאוּ עִמָּהּ מִבֵּית אָבִיהָ לְבֵית בַּעְלָהּ — מֵתָה, לֹא זָכָה הַבַּעַל בִּדְבָרִים הַלָּלוּ. מִשּׁוּם רַבִּי נָתָן אָמְרוּ: זָכָה הַבַּעַל בִּדְבָרִים הַלָּלוּ.",
   "en": "§ The mishna further taught that if the daughter «married, the husband has more» rights «than» her father, «as he consumes» the produce of her property. «The Sages taught» in a baraita: If the father «wrote for her» in her marriage contract that he was providing «produce, clothing, and vessels that would come with her» as a dowry «from her father’s house to her husband’s house,» and «she died» during the betrothal period, «the husband does not have the right to these objects. They said in the name of Rabbi Natan: The husband does have the right to these objects.»"
  }
 ],
